<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Halland</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Halland is a province on the west coast of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, formerly held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>. It passed to Sweden through seventeenth-century treaties, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-roskilde">Treaty of Roskilde</a> of 1658 concluded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-x-gustav">Charles X Gustav</a>. Its acquisition helped establish the boundaries of modern Sweden during the expansion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/halland.jpg" alt="Halland" width="320" height="246" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peter Wÿchman · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Geografisk_karta_%C3%B6ver_landsv%C3%A4garna_genom_Halland.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
